---
description: NetSpider project rules (canonical source - AGENTS.md)
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow AGENTS.md in the repository root: it is the canonical instruction file (layout, build/test, code style,
changelog and PR rules, privacy, releases). Read it before changing anything.

Always:
- Add a user-facing line under `## [Unreleased]` in CHANGELOG.md for every user-visible change, exactly as described
  in CHANGELOG-GUIDELINES.md (fixed categories Breaking, New, Improved, Fixed, Security, Removed, Deprecated, in that
  order; one sentence ending with a period). Otherwise the PR needs the `skip-changelog` label.
- Use Conventional Commit PR titles and commit messages: `type(scope)!: description`.
- Run `dotnet test NetworkScan.slnx` before pushing.

Never:
- push to main, edit released changelog sections, bump versions or create tags;
- put real names, IPs, MACs, host names or user names in code, tests, screenshots or docs (use `--demo --hide-banners`).
